Subject: [PATCH] Classifier: through cut (type 1 on any domain), topology,
 whole spheres in the test models

Type 1 also when the TO is the domain cut by its own outline along an axis
(IoU >= 0.8; knuckle Case 1: 0.87), tested after height field and sandwich.
Sandwich again requires a sheet. Topology reported: components, enclosed
cavities, tunnels (Euler number). Plate and rod limits separated (both 0.45;
0.67 for plates added plate noise at rod junctions). Test models: whole
spheres (makeSphere's default is a hemisphere); mass model of three
non-collinear lobes (two coaxial spheres are axisymmetric).
run_classify.py: 11 models x 8 variants pass.

